   "id": "kospi-plunge-ai-fears",
   "group": "Korea",
   "headline": "Seoul stocks drop more than 5% as chip shares lead the fall",
   "when": "Thu 5 Nov · Seoul close",
   "what": "The KOSPI closed at 5,383.80, down 5.28%. A five-minute pause in program trading was triggered in the morning. Samsung Electronics fell 7.57% to 201,500 won and SK hynix fell 9.46% to 1.26 million won. Foreigners sold a net 3.39 trillion won of shares, while individuals and institutions bought. The won was quoted at 1,342.1 per dollar. Analysts tied the fall to worry that a Democratic Congress will tighten rules on AI data centres.",
   "why": "Korea is 17.2% of your portfolio, mostly SCBKEQTG. That fund is priced at its 3 Nov NAV this morning, so Thursday's fall is not yet in your dashboard. The dashboard refreshes again at 11:30, when newer fund NAVs usually arrive. Wall Street fell further after Seoul closed, which is a risk for Friday's open.",
