   "headline": "US stocks slump as AI and chip shares are sold hard",
   "when": "Thu 5 Nov · New York",
   "what": "Late in the morning the S&P 500 was down about 3.2% and the Nasdaq about 5%, on track for the worst S&P drop since April 2025. Your dashboard's closing tiles show the S&P 500 down 4.36% and Nasdaq down 5.52%. Nvidia lost about 8 to 9% and AMD about 15 to 16%. The chip index fell as much as 11.2%. The 10-year Treasury yield eased to 4.84% from 4.90%. A month ago it was above 5.30%.",
